## Lookup: read types before prose

| Need | Read | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| A UIKit component's props | `node_modules/@bloomneo/uikit/dist/types/index.d.ts` | ~1.3k tok, complete public API |
| An AppKit module's API | `node_modules/@bloomneo/appkit/dist/<module>/index.d.ts` | small, per-module |
| A contract route (method, path, schemas, auth) | `src/contracts/*.contract.ts` | the source of truth for both sides |
| A plain-router route this app serves | `src/web/shared/api-routes.ts` | generated, always current |
| Contracts, the client, `bloom check` | `node_modules/@bloomneo/bloom/llms.txt` | short |
| Long-form explanation | `docs/` | ~23k tok — last resort, not first |

The `.d.ts` is authoritative and matches the installed version. The prose does
not always. **Do not guess a prop name — the type file is cheaper to read than
the mistake is to debug.**

## Never write a bare string where a type exists

Every expensive mistake made in this codebase was a plausible, wrong string
that compiled cleanly. Strings are the failure surface.

```ts
// ✗ compiles, 404s at runtime
fetch('/api/user')

// ✓ a contract: path, params and response type all come from it
import { client } from '@/shared/client';
import { getWelcomeByName } from '@contracts/welcome.contract';
const hello = await client.call(getWelcomeByName, { params: { name: 'Ada' } });

// ✓ a plain router: compile error if the route does not exist
import { api } from '@/shared/api';
api.get('/api/user/admin/users')
```

- **New API routes are contracts.** Declare the route in
  `src/contracts/<name>.contract.ts` with `defineRoute` (from
  `@bloomneo/bloom`) — `auth` is required: `'public'`, `'user'`, `'apiToken'`
  or `{ roles: ['admin.system'] }`. Serve it from
  `src/api/features/<name>/<name>.route.ts` with
  `export default await contractRouter([route(contract, handler)])` (from
  `@bloomneo/appkit/server`). Call it with `client.call(contract, input)`. A
  contract file imports only `zod` and `@bloomneo/bloom` — both builds
  compile it.
- **API calls** → `client.call` (contracts) or `api.get/post/patch/delete`
  from `@/shared/api` (plain routers). Never call `fetch` directly. The
  clients own the base URL, the JWT, the frontend key and the error shape.
- **Routes** → typed by `ApiRoute`, generated from the route files by
  `npm run gen:routes` (runs automatically on `npm run dev`).
- **Roles** → `role.level` pairs, e.g. `'admin.system'`. The full list is in
  `prisma/seeding/user.seed.js`, not invented. (auth layer)

## Backend conventions

- The API router is `createApiRouter` from `@bloomneo/appkit/server`
  (mounted in `server.ts`). There is no router file in the app to edit: a
  feature folder with a `<name>.route.ts` IS the registration.
- **Every route has an auth decision**: the contract's `auth`, an
  `auth.requireLoginToken()` / `requireUserRoles()` guard, or
  `export const isPublic = true` in a plain router. `npx bloom check` fails
  on a route file without one — run it after adding routes.
- In a contract handler, don't re-check auth or re-validate input: `route()`
  already applied the contract. Return the body; throw `error.notFound()` etc.
- Get instances via `xxxClass.get()` — never `new SomethingClass()`.
- Wrap async handlers: `error.asyncRoute(async (req, res) => { … })`.
- **One route file per feature**: `features/<name>/<name>.route.ts` and no
  other. A second `.route.ts` in the same folder is silently ignored — the
  endpoint will 404 with no warning. Need a second surface? New feature folder.
- `res` inside `asyncRoute` is typed as `{ status, json }` only. `.send()` and
  `.end()` do not compile, so a bodyless 204 is unreachable — return
  `res.json({ ok: true })`.
- Ownership goes in the WHERE clause, not just a session check. Use
  `updateMany`/`deleteMany` with `{ id, userId }` so another user's id cannot
  be passed in.

## Frontend conventions

- A file's location is its URL. `features/todo/pages/index.tsx` → `/todo`.
  Prefix with `_` to keep a file out of routing. The router is `<PageRouter>`
  from `@bloomneo/uikit/router`; the app's only routing code is the glob in
  `src/web/pages.ts`.
- The signed-in shell is uikit's `AppShell` (in
  `shared/DashboardLayoutRoute.tsx`, auth layer). Don't hand-roll a sidebar.
- Adding a sidebar entry means editing `shared/nav.base.ts` (auth layer) —
  layers contribute their own `nav.<layer>.ts`.
- Never set a `theme-*` class on `<html>` by hand — `ThemeProvider` strips any
  class it did not set, and the change vanishes with no error.

## Database

SQLite (`DATABASE_URL=file:./dev.db`) is the zero-setup default. Production,
and any multi-tenant app, runs on Postgres with `BLOOM_DB_TENANT=rls` — appkit
scopes queries to the caller's tenant with row-level security, and
`npx bloom check` fails on a tenant table without it.

## After changing the Prisma schema

Restart the dev server. `prisma generate` updates the client on disk, but the
running process keeps the old one — new columns read as `undefined` with no
error. This has cost more debugging time than any other single issue here.
